          body: "One of the women who watch the crucifixion from afar (27:55–56), who are present at the burial (27:61), and who come to the tomb at dawn on the first day of the week (28:1). In Matthew’s account she and “the other Mary” encounter the angel, are told Jesus has risen, and meet the risen Jesus himself on their way to tell the disciples. They grasp his feet and worship him. Mary Magdalene is the first named witness of the resurrection in Matthew’s gospel.",
